1
00:00:01,958 --> 00:00:04,874
[indistinct chattering]

2
00:00:07,224 --> 00:00:10,358
You clean up very nicely,
if you don't mind me saying so.

3
00:00:10,445 --> 00:00:12,273
I don't mind you saying so.
Thanks.

4
00:00:15,102 --> 00:00:18,496
You look pretty much the same
as you always look.

5
00:00:18,583 --> 00:00:20,890
- Oh. Really?
- Yes.

6
00:00:20,977 --> 00:00:24,154
- This is my date outfit.
- Really?

7
00:00:24,241 --> 00:00:27,070
Is this your first date? I mean,
um, since your wife died?

8
00:00:27,157 --> 00:00:28,985
Do I seem out of practice?

9
00:00:29,072 --> 00:00:30,769
- Hi.
- Hi.

10
00:00:30,856 --> 00:00:32,423
Uh, my name's Gerard. I'll be
your server this evening.

11
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:33,685
Would you like
to hear our specials?

12
00:00:33,772 --> 00:00:35,296
I'm sorry
to interrupt, Gerard

13
00:00:35,383 --> 00:00:37,472
but I'm getting a message
from, uh, your mother.

14
00:00:38,647 --> 00:00:41,476
- A Janet no, um, Janis.
- Yes.

15
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:44,522
Um..

16
00:00:45,741 --> 00:00:47,830
'I'm sorry for your loss.'

17
00:00:47,917 --> 00:00:49,962
She's happy now.

18
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:54,532
And she wants you to know that
she sends her deepest love.

19
00:00:54,619 --> 00:00:56,926
And, um..

20
00:00:57,013 --> 00:01:02,192
...your uncle, Ed says,
"roll tide."

21
00:01:02,279 --> 00:01:06,109
Does that mean anything
to you, "roll tide"?

22
00:01:06,196 --> 00:01:09,243
[Gerard]
'My mother's brother Edward.
He died five years ago.'

23
00:01:09,330 --> 00:01:11,419
He was a tight end
at Alabama in the '60s.

24
00:01:11,506 --> 00:01:12,985
Oh.

25
00:01:13,073 --> 00:01:14,944
Uh, they're called
the Crimson Tide.

26
00:01:15,031 --> 00:01:17,207
Uh, that's their rallying cry,
"roll tide."

27
00:01:17,294 --> 00:01:18,556
Oh.

28
00:01:18,643 --> 00:01:20,080
Well, uh, I'd like to have

29
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:23,083
the soup du jour
and the lamb, medium

30
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:25,868
and the arugula salad
and the fish for the lady.

31
00:01:25,955 --> 00:01:28,566
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

32
00:01:28,653 --> 00:01:29,828
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

33
00:01:29,915 --> 00:01:31,003
Thanks.

34
00:01:33,702 --> 00:01:35,007
[clears throat]

35
00:01:37,488 --> 00:01:40,796
- What?
- Oh, come on.

36
00:01:40,883 --> 00:01:43,233
You're so ferocious
in your lack of faith.

37
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:46,802
I mean, is it so hard to imagine
that I'm not putting on an act?

38
00:01:46,889 --> 00:01:49,935
That, that I really am
what I say I am?

39
00:01:50,022 --> 00:01:52,590
His mother sent a message.
I'm meant to help. That's all.

40
00:01:54,114 --> 00:01:55,767
It happens to me
all the time.

41
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,248
Okay.

42
00:02:00,337 --> 00:02:02,644
I'm sorry.

43
00:02:02,731 --> 00:02:04,733
Roll tide.

44
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,039
[alert chimes]

45
00:02:10,304 --> 00:02:13,089
[telephone ringing]

46
00:02:13,176 --> 00:02:15,091
[sighs]

47
00:02:15,178 --> 00:02:17,528
Bad guys just
keep on coming, huh?

48
00:02:17,615 --> 00:02:20,009
I hate the internet.

49
00:02:20,096 --> 00:02:22,229
Listen, if you like,
I can deal. You go.

50
00:02:22,316 --> 00:02:25,188
No, it's okay.
It's just a web alert

51
00:02:25,275 --> 00:02:28,800
for when a name
we're interested in pops up.

52
00:02:28,887 --> 00:02:30,454
[clicking mouse]

53
00:02:36,634 --> 00:02:38,506
Wayne?

54
00:02:38,593 --> 00:02:39,811
What is it?

55
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,032
Oh.

56
00:02:47,863 --> 00:02:50,822
This is not good.

57
00:02:50,909 --> 00:02:52,737
Relax, it's,
it's just a hoax.

58
00:02:52,824 --> 00:02:54,826
It's staged,
almost certainly.

59
00:03:01,485 --> 00:03:03,966
[intense music]

60
00:03:05,533 --> 00:03:06,795
[Van Pelt]
'Oh, my God!'

61
00:03:09,537 --> 00:03:10,973
[gasps]

62
00:03:15,630 --> 00:03:17,153
- I didn't put-- uh, no.
- Yes.

63
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:19,199
[laughing]
No. no.

64
00:03:19,286 --> 00:03:21,679
- You went to jail, really?
- Yes, I did.

65
00:03:21,766 --> 00:03:23,594
- What's so hard to believe?
- For how long?

66
00:03:23,681 --> 00:03:25,944
I was there for two days
and two very luxurious nights.

67
00:03:26,031 --> 00:03:28,425
Uh-huh. Yeah.
And how'd you get out?

68
00:03:28,512 --> 00:03:30,079
- I just escaped.
- Uh-huh.

69
00:03:30,166 --> 00:03:31,820
I don't believe you
for one second.

70
00:03:31,907 --> 00:03:34,605
It wasn't, it wasn't that
difficult. It's all timing.

71
00:03:34,692 --> 00:03:36,433
Uh-huh.

72
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:39,088
- I'm not kidding. Okay.
- Uh-huh.

73
00:03:39,175 --> 00:03:41,003
Excuse me.
I have to go to the bathroom.

74
00:03:44,093 --> 00:03:46,182
[laughing]

75
00:03:47,139 --> 00:03:48,271
Ah, thank you.

76
00:03:52,362 --> 00:03:54,016
[sighs]

77
00:04:07,943 --> 00:04:10,815
[instrumental music]

78
00:04:33,055 --> 00:04:35,927
[indistinct chattering]

79
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,715
[sighs]
Hey.

80
00:04:44,936 --> 00:04:46,373
'Kristina, um..'

81
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:47,983
[cellphone rings]

82
00:04:48,070 --> 00:04:49,985
Oh. I'm so sorry.

83
00:04:51,987 --> 00:04:54,294
[beep]
It's work. Hello.

84
00:04:54,381 --> 00:04:57,993
Jane, you need to come
to the office right now.

85
00:04:59,951 --> 00:05:02,563
[intense music]

86
00:05:07,176 --> 00:05:09,918
[theme music]

87
00:05:19,797 --> 00:05:22,365
[instrumental music]

88
00:05:27,762 --> 00:05:30,634
[gasps and whimpers]

89
00:05:30,721 --> 00:05:33,202
[screaming]

90
00:05:34,508 --> 00:05:36,205
[video fast-forwarding]

91
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,905
[music continues]

92
00:05:42,820 --> 00:05:44,431
it was posted on the internet
an hour ago

93
00:05:44,518 --> 00:05:46,171
on a popular notice board.

94
00:05:46,258 --> 00:05:48,696
There's a message
that goes with it.

95
00:05:48,783 --> 00:05:50,741
"I am becoming
what I was meant to be.

96
00:05:50,828 --> 00:05:53,483
'Your children's children
will worship me."'

97
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,137
We don't know when or where
the video was made.

98
00:05:55,224 --> 00:05:56,660
There appears to be
an '08 Silverado

99
00:05:56,747 --> 00:05:58,096
parked outside the house

100
00:05:58,183 --> 00:06:00,708
so it's gotta be
at least that recent.

101
00:06:00,795 --> 00:06:02,405
Has Red John made videos

102
00:06:02,492 --> 00:06:03,798
or issued statements
like this before?

103
00:06:03,885 --> 00:06:05,887
- No.
- Oh, thank you.

104
00:06:05,974 --> 00:06:07,889
Excuse me.
Sorry to interrupt.

105
00:06:07,976 --> 00:06:11,327
Oh. Hi, Kristina.
Uh, good to see you.

106
00:06:11,414 --> 00:06:14,417
Yeah. That poor girl.

107
00:06:14,504 --> 00:06:16,201
Yeah, yeah.

108
00:06:16,288 --> 00:06:18,160
For what it's worth
I'm getting a sense

109
00:06:18,247 --> 00:06:20,380
that she died very recently.

110
00:06:20,467 --> 00:06:24,427
Her body will be discovered
very soon. She's near water.

111
00:06:27,778 --> 00:06:30,215
Does this feel like
Red John to you?

112
00:06:30,302 --> 00:06:32,783
Uh, I'm not getting
a read on that.

113
00:06:32,870 --> 00:06:34,959
The whole internet aspect is
interesting, though, isn't it?

114
00:06:35,046 --> 00:06:36,613
I mean,
why put it up there?

115
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:41,488
This clip's had over a million
viewers. A desire for fame?

116
00:06:41,575 --> 00:06:43,054
[Hightower]
'Patrick, you're
being very quiet.'

117
00:06:43,141 --> 00:06:44,621
What are you thinking?

118
00:06:44,708 --> 00:06:46,580
Uh, I'd have to see
the crime scene.

119
00:06:46,667 --> 00:06:49,060
CHP just reported
a homicide in the Bay Area.

120
00:06:49,147 --> 00:06:50,453
'Smiley face on the wall.'

121
00:06:50,540 --> 00:06:52,542
'College student
named Marley Sparrow.'

122
00:06:52,629 --> 00:06:55,066
'Roommate found her, called it
in about a half-hour ago.'

123
00:06:55,153 --> 00:06:56,154
Let's get ready to go.

124
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:59,810
- Bay area?
- Uh, yes.

125
00:06:59,897 --> 00:07:02,334
That is close to water.
That's, uh, that's uncanny.

126
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:04,859
Oh, come on.
That's pretty good.

127
00:07:04,946 --> 00:07:07,644
I am feeling a strong connection
to this case somehow.

128
00:07:07,731 --> 00:07:10,081
Madeline,
can we have a word, please?

129
00:07:10,168 --> 00:07:11,474
Yeah.

130
00:07:11,561 --> 00:07:12,562
[Hightower]
'Excuse us.'

131
00:07:15,957 --> 00:07:17,959
She's gonna ask
if she can come along with us.

132
00:07:18,046 --> 00:07:21,266
Now obviously, that's your call.
But I hope that you refuse

133
00:07:21,353 --> 00:07:23,834
because I won't work with her.
I will quit.

134
00:07:23,921 --> 00:07:26,881
What's your objection?
If she can help us, why not?

135
00:07:26,968 --> 00:07:29,884
Nothing she says
is more than clever guesswork.

136
00:07:29,971 --> 00:07:33,235
So she has essentially
the same skills as you.

137
00:07:33,322 --> 00:07:34,541
Without all the drama.

138
00:07:36,238 --> 00:07:37,369
What's the deal?

139
00:07:39,197 --> 00:07:40,503
Red John is mine.

140
00:07:43,767 --> 00:07:46,248
Okay. Okay, I hear you.

141
00:07:46,335 --> 00:07:47,336
[whispers]
Thank you.

142
00:07:47,423 --> 00:07:48,468
I'm sorry to interrupt.

143
00:07:48,555 --> 00:07:50,121
- Oh, please.
- Uh..

144
00:07:52,559 --> 00:07:55,475
Um, I was going to offer
my services

145
00:07:55,562 --> 00:07:57,346
but I get the sense
Mr. Jane is telling you

146
00:07:57,433 --> 00:07:58,565
that he won't work with me.

147
00:08:00,828 --> 00:08:03,874
The last thing I want to do
is upset this investigation

148
00:08:03,961 --> 00:08:05,659
but if I have any more
feelings about the case

149
00:08:05,746 --> 00:08:06,747
could I call you?

150
00:08:06,834 --> 00:08:08,705
Of course, Kristina.

151
00:08:08,792 --> 00:08:11,055
Always be glad
to hear your thoughts.

152
00:08:11,142 --> 00:08:12,274
- Have a goodnight.
- Thank you.

153
00:08:15,233 --> 00:08:16,496
[whispers]
Okay.

154
00:08:19,977 --> 00:08:21,849
- Listen, uh, I--
- I completely understand.

155
00:08:21,936 --> 00:08:24,460
- No hard feelings.
- Okay.

156
00:08:26,897 --> 00:08:28,769
That was an unusual date,
though, huh?

157
00:08:28,856 --> 00:08:30,292
- Yes, very.
- Thank you.

158
00:08:31,946 --> 00:08:33,164
I'll see you soon,
I hope.

159
00:08:34,731 --> 00:08:35,950
[elevator bell rings]

160
00:08:36,037 --> 00:08:37,647
[elevator doors open]

161
00:08:37,734 --> 00:08:39,823
- Um, would you--
- Oh, yeah, sure.

162
00:08:41,303 --> 00:08:42,391
Oh.

163
00:08:46,351 --> 00:08:47,527
- Bye.
- Bye.

164
00:08:50,399 --> 00:08:53,010
[indistinct radio chatter]

165
00:08:57,711 --> 00:09:00,235
[camera shutter clicking]

166
00:09:00,322 --> 00:09:01,584
Guys, give me
a minute, please.

167
00:09:04,239 --> 00:09:05,327
Thank you.

168
00:09:08,330 --> 00:09:11,246
[instrumental music]

169
00:09:22,953 --> 00:09:25,434
[whispers]
Hey, Marley. We'll get
this sorted out for you.

170
00:09:27,349 --> 00:09:29,786
[music continues]

171
00:09:45,759 --> 00:09:48,065
[indistinct radio chatter]

172
00:09:50,328 --> 00:09:52,330
Hey, hey,
Patrick Jane.

173
00:09:52,417 --> 00:09:54,419
Long time.

174
00:09:54,506 --> 00:09:56,596
'So, que pasa,dude?'

175
00:09:56,683 --> 00:09:58,859
My people need
to do their thing.

176
00:09:58,946 --> 00:10:00,948
I won't be long.

177
00:10:01,035 --> 00:10:02,210
Oh.

178
00:10:04,081 --> 00:10:05,430
[clears throat]

179
00:10:08,738 --> 00:10:13,003
'You hoovering up the, uh,
ol' psychic ectoplasm?'

180
00:10:13,090 --> 00:10:15,745
[makes buzzing sounds]

181
00:10:15,832 --> 00:10:18,705
Yeah, that's exactly
what I'm doing.

182
00:10:18,792 --> 00:10:21,316
We have a schedule to keep,
amigo.Tick-tock.

183
00:10:21,403 --> 00:10:22,796
Sooner you're done
fooling around

184
00:10:22,883 --> 00:10:24,841
sooner my people can find
actual clues.

185
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:29,063
She's from Iowa.

186
00:10:29,150 --> 00:10:31,979
She played the guitar.
She liked dark chocolate

187
00:10:32,066 --> 00:10:34,242
sudoku and snowboarding.

188
00:10:35,722 --> 00:10:39,464
Shy, but strong.
Honorable, modest.

189
00:10:39,551 --> 00:10:40,988
Didn't drink or smoke.

190
00:10:42,511 --> 00:10:44,121
Parents died
when she was very young.

191
00:10:44,208 --> 00:10:46,297
And after college,
she wanted to go into family law

192
00:10:46,384 --> 00:10:48,691
and help foster kids
like herself.

193
00:10:48,778 --> 00:10:52,564
Or become a singer.
She hadn't made up her mind yet.

194
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:55,480
Yeah, that's great, dude.
But where's Red John?

195
00:10:55,567 --> 00:10:57,221
Oh, this wasn't Red John.

196
00:10:57,308 --> 00:10:58,658
So you say.

197
00:11:01,095 --> 00:11:02,313
So I say.

198
00:11:05,969 --> 00:11:08,189
[whispers]
Jerk.

199
00:11:08,276 --> 00:11:10,147
Oh, make sure
you have your people

200
00:11:10,234 --> 00:11:13,585
send those papers and journals
to the CBI office.

201
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,675
- Will do.
- Thank you.

202
00:11:17,546 --> 00:11:19,853
[indistinct chattering]

203
00:11:24,509 --> 00:11:25,902
[sniffles]

204
00:11:34,563 --> 00:11:36,086
[female #1]
'Marley was the best.'

205
00:11:36,173 --> 00:11:38,001
'The best person.'

206
00:11:38,088 --> 00:11:39,829
A beautiful soul.

207
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:42,876
[Lisbon]
'Ruth, you found her body, yes?'

208
00:11:42,963 --> 00:11:44,704
When you entered your house,
did you notice

209
00:11:44,791 --> 00:11:46,401
anything unusual
before you found the body?

210
00:11:46,488 --> 00:11:48,011
Something missing
or out of place?

211
00:11:48,098 --> 00:11:49,796
No, I don't think so.

212
00:11:49,883 --> 00:11:52,755
- How long had you been gone?
- Two days, snowboarding.

213
00:11:52,842 --> 00:11:55,845
Marley was supposed to come
but then her boyfriend

214
00:11:55,932 --> 00:11:57,978
was coming over to see her,
so she stayed.

215
00:11:58,065 --> 00:12:00,415
- Boyfriend's name?
- Grady Shipp.

216
00:12:00,502 --> 00:12:02,199
He's a policeman
in San Francisco.

217
00:12:03,766 --> 00:12:06,900
They've been dating
for, like, a month.

218
00:12:06,987 --> 00:12:08,858
Okay. What was he like?
Nice guy?

219
00:12:08,945 --> 00:12:10,773
Marley really liked him
a lot.

220
00:12:10,860 --> 00:12:12,557
Said he was super nice.

221
00:12:12,644 --> 00:12:14,646
But I don't know.
We never actually met him.

222
00:12:14,734 --> 00:12:15,996
No?

223
00:12:16,083 --> 00:12:18,433
She'd go to his place,
mostly.

224
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:21,523
And when he came by here,
he'd wait for her in his car.

225
00:12:21,610 --> 00:12:23,264
Weird, no?

226
00:12:23,351 --> 00:12:26,006
I think Marley was
a bit embarrassed

227
00:12:26,093 --> 00:12:28,704
for hooking up with a cop,
you know?

228
00:12:28,791 --> 00:12:30,575
So she kept him
on the down low.

229
00:12:30,662 --> 00:12:32,534
Embarrassed, why?

230
00:12:32,621 --> 00:12:35,450
Marley was cool.

231
00:12:35,537 --> 00:12:38,279
And, well, cops are sort of
nerds with guns, aren't they?

232
00:12:38,366 --> 00:12:40,324
Ruth, hello?

233
00:12:41,673 --> 00:12:42,674
No offense.

234
00:12:44,633 --> 00:12:46,461
[laughing]
Sorry.

235
00:12:46,548 --> 00:12:48,115
'Marley sparrow?'

236
00:12:48,202 --> 00:12:51,640
Yes, I was her academic advisor
for two semesters.

237
00:12:51,727 --> 00:12:53,294
Nice enough girl,

238
00:12:53,381 --> 00:12:56,340
but not as clever
as she likes to think she is.

239
00:12:56,427 --> 00:12:58,342
But none of 'em are,
are they? Ha!

240
00:12:58,429 --> 00:13:00,649
Did you notice any changes
in her behavior recently?

241
00:13:00,736 --> 00:13:03,304
No. But nor do I
pay close attention.

242
00:13:03,391 --> 00:13:05,523
They're all empty vessels
to be filled with knowledge.

243
00:13:05,610 --> 00:13:08,526
Here is
a horrible coincidence.

244
00:13:08,613 --> 00:13:12,400
Last semester, I taught
a criminology elective.

245
00:13:12,487 --> 00:13:17,666
Murder, myth and marketing,
the serial killer as commodity.

246
00:13:17,753 --> 00:13:20,364
Red John
was actually mentioned

247
00:13:20,451 --> 00:13:22,845
in our class discussions.
Isn't that eerie?

248
00:13:22,932 --> 00:13:24,760
Who mentioned him?
What'd they say?

249
00:13:24,847 --> 00:13:26,718
Oh, damned if I know.
It was eight or nine months ago.

250
00:13:26,806 --> 00:13:28,372
Do you have a student list
from the class?

251
00:13:28,459 --> 00:13:31,419
You know, I do.
I do. Somewhere.

252
00:13:33,464 --> 00:13:34,857
[lowered voice]
I do.

253
00:13:34,944 --> 00:13:36,554
We would love
to get a look at that list.

254
00:13:39,862 --> 00:13:41,168
[indistinct chattering]

255
00:13:41,255 --> 00:13:42,909
Thanks.

256
00:13:42,996 --> 00:13:44,606
So there's no Grady Shipp
with any San Fran Police Agency.

257
00:13:44,693 --> 00:13:45,825
There's no
Grady Shipp, period.

258
00:13:45,912 --> 00:13:47,087
There was
a Grady Shipp once.

259
00:13:47,174 --> 00:13:48,697
He killed and ate
his next-door neighbors

260
00:13:48,784 --> 00:13:51,221
in little rock back in the '90s.
He was lethally injected

261
00:13:51,308 --> 00:13:53,136
by the state of Arkansas
in '02.

262
00:13:53,223 --> 00:13:55,095
Huh. So Marley's boyfriend
doesn't want anybody

263
00:13:55,182 --> 00:13:57,662
to see his face, and he named
himself after a cannibal.

264
00:13:57,749 --> 00:13:59,099
'That's two strikes
against him.'

265
00:13:59,186 --> 00:14:00,927
Shame we don't have
a name or a description.

266
00:14:01,014 --> 00:14:03,059
The roommate, Ruth, said that
he never got out of his car.

267
00:14:03,146 --> 00:14:04,669
Maybe we can get
a make and model from her.

268
00:14:04,756 --> 00:14:07,629
Grady Shipp.

269
00:14:07,716 --> 00:14:10,893
In 1989, he did a 6-month spell
in the same wing

270
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:12,634
at Lompoc as Orval Tanner.

271
00:14:12,721 --> 00:14:14,549
- Orval Tanner?
- Red John's friend.

272
00:14:14,636 --> 00:14:17,813
You have the entire Lompoc
Prison registry in your head?

273
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:20,120
Well, only
the relevant sections.

274
00:14:20,207 --> 00:14:21,730
[Lisbon]
'Wh-what does it mean?
Is it a joke?'

275
00:14:21,817 --> 00:14:23,340
[Rigsby]
'Marley's boyfriend
is Red John.'

276
00:14:23,427 --> 00:14:24,776
[Cho]
'That doesn't make
any sense.'

277
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,825
In the hunt for this beast
known as "Red John."

278
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,960
well, he--
he's not a beast, Jackie.

279
00:14:34,047 --> 00:14:35,526
He's a human being.

280
00:14:35,613 --> 00:14:37,441
Now he has done
terrible things

281
00:14:37,528 --> 00:14:39,443
but he is still
capable of redemption..

282
00:14:40,705 --> 00:14:41,881
...like all of us.

283
00:14:45,580 --> 00:14:49,105
Red John..

284
00:14:49,192 --> 00:14:50,715
...if you're listening
to us now

285
00:14:50,802 --> 00:14:54,328
I urge you to reach out
and get help.

286
00:14:54,415 --> 00:14:56,808
You can change.

287
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:59,115
[indistinct chattering]

288
00:15:01,161 --> 00:15:03,859
[instrumental music]

289
00:15:14,870 --> 00:15:16,437
What the hell
are you thinking?

290
00:15:16,524 --> 00:15:18,569
Don't you understand
who you're dealing with?

291
00:15:18,656 --> 00:15:20,006
I do understand, yes.

292
00:15:20,093 --> 00:15:22,617
No, you don't. Clearly,
you don't understand.

293
00:15:22,704 --> 00:15:24,314
I asked Miss Frye here

294
00:15:24,401 --> 00:15:26,360
so that I could fully
express my deep dismay.

295
00:15:26,447 --> 00:15:28,057
I was speaking
from the heart.

296
00:15:28,144 --> 00:15:31,060
That may be, but you were also
hustling for business.

297
00:15:31,147 --> 00:15:33,671
'And that's okay, but you
present me now with a problem.'

298
00:15:35,456 --> 00:15:37,501
We don't have any obligation
to protect you, but--

299
00:15:37,588 --> 00:15:40,200
I wasn't asking for protection.
It's completely unnecessary.

300
00:15:40,287 --> 00:15:41,810
Red John
is not coming after me.

301
00:15:41,897 --> 00:15:45,074
Are you blind?
You've done exactly what I did.

302
00:15:45,161 --> 00:15:47,990
I went on television and talked
about him as though I knew him

303
00:15:48,077 --> 00:15:49,774
and he killed
my wife and child.

304
00:15:49,861 --> 00:15:53,691
Patrick, he was punishing you
because you lied about him.

305
00:15:53,778 --> 00:15:56,868
'I was telling the truth.
He won't take offense with me.'

306
00:15:56,956 --> 00:15:58,479
He might even listen
to what I said.

307
00:15:58,566 --> 00:15:59,959
In fact,
I-I believe he will.

308
00:16:02,091 --> 00:16:04,311
People do change, Patrick.
It's possible.

309
00:16:06,704 --> 00:16:09,316
Agent Hightower, I'm truly
sorry for dismaying you.

310
00:16:11,753 --> 00:16:13,842
Now if you'll excuse me,
I have some other appointments.

311
00:16:19,630 --> 00:16:21,893
[inhales deeply]
She needs 24-hour protection.

312
00:16:21,981 --> 00:16:24,853
The best that you can provide.

313
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:26,768
The Sac PD
Special Protection Unit

314
00:16:26,855 --> 00:16:29,379
will provide security,
the CBI will be on the inside

315
00:16:29,466 --> 00:16:32,078
bodyguarding Miss Frye. Jane
and I will take the first shift.

316
00:16:32,165 --> 00:16:34,254
The next 24-hour rotation
will be split among us

317
00:16:34,341 --> 00:16:36,169
alternating with
the Sparrow case.

318
00:16:36,256 --> 00:16:38,258
Well, we're gonna have to stop
protecting her sooner or later.

319
00:16:38,345 --> 00:16:40,260
That's when he'll go for her.
He'll just wait.

320
00:16:40,347 --> 00:16:41,696
Van Pelt,
what do you got?

321
00:16:41,783 --> 00:16:43,698
We're looking
for Grady Shipp, right?

322
00:16:43,785 --> 00:16:45,526
This is
Marley's address book.

323
00:16:45,613 --> 00:16:48,007
That's different writing. Maybe
that's Grady Shipp himself.

324
00:16:48,094 --> 00:16:49,834
- Can I?
- 'Keep digging.'

325
00:16:49,921 --> 00:16:51,271
Rigsby, take Cho with you.
Check it out.

326
00:16:51,358 --> 00:16:52,663
Yeah, you got it.

327
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,410
[clank]

328
00:17:00,497 --> 00:17:01,629
Hello?

329
00:17:05,285 --> 00:17:07,026
[door creaking]

330
00:17:12,292 --> 00:17:14,946
[flapping sounds]

331
00:17:19,734 --> 00:17:21,127
Hello?

332
00:17:23,172 --> 00:17:26,045
[intense music]

333
00:17:40,755 --> 00:17:42,104
[sighs]

334
00:17:44,324 --> 00:17:46,935
[music continues]

335
00:17:52,245 --> 00:17:53,376
- Blood.
- Yep.

336
00:17:56,423 --> 00:17:58,990
[exhales]
Pig's blood, maybe.

337
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:02,168
For practice?

338
00:18:02,255 --> 00:18:03,908
[footsteps approaching

339
00:18:03,995 --> 00:18:07,434
[gunshots]

340
00:18:07,521 --> 00:18:09,088
[panting]

341
00:18:10,828 --> 00:18:13,396
[intense music]

342
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:16,312
Police! Stop!

343
00:18:18,749 --> 00:18:20,360
Hey! Stop!

344
00:18:31,022 --> 00:18:33,112
[engine revving]

345
00:18:33,721 --> 00:18:34,809
Damn!

346
00:18:36,811 --> 00:18:38,160
I'll call it in.

347
00:18:38,247 --> 00:18:40,684
[panting]

348
00:18:45,428 --> 00:18:47,343
What is it?

349
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:49,998
A lens cap.
Interesting.

350
00:18:50,085 --> 00:18:51,826
Practicing
the Red John symbol

351
00:18:51,913 --> 00:18:54,524
and not just watching us
pursue him

352
00:18:54,611 --> 00:18:56,396
but filming the pursuit.

353
00:18:56,483 --> 00:18:58,180
What does it mean?

354
00:18:58,267 --> 00:19:00,835
It means Marley Sparrow's
killer loves cameras.

355
00:19:00,922 --> 00:19:03,794
He's a voyeur, a fanboy,
a slasher movie geek.

356
00:19:03,881 --> 00:19:05,405
Huh.

357
00:19:05,492 --> 00:19:08,321
Great. But where does
that take us now? Like in a car?

358
00:19:08,408 --> 00:19:10,888
Well, try
the campus film club.

359
00:19:10,975 --> 00:19:12,063
Alright.

360
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:16,981
Nice place, huh?
Tasteful.

361
00:19:17,068 --> 00:19:19,419
To me, it looks like we're
about to pay way too much money

362
00:19:19,506 --> 00:19:20,463
to get our legs waxed.

363
00:19:20,550 --> 00:19:22,422
- Hmm.
- Hi.

364
00:19:22,509 --> 00:19:24,511
I was just making some lunch.
Would you like something to eat?

365
00:19:24,598 --> 00:19:25,860
Sure, thanks.

366
00:19:25,947 --> 00:19:28,384
I'm good.
Thanks.

367
00:19:28,471 --> 00:19:31,213
Patrick, uh,
on reflection

368
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:33,868
I'm truly sorry
for the situation I put you in.

369
00:19:33,955 --> 00:19:35,174
I hadn't thought through
your involvement.

370
00:19:35,261 --> 00:19:37,176
Alright, alright.
I-I-I'll eat some lunch.

371
00:19:37,263 --> 00:19:38,481
Just please
don't make a fuss.

372
00:19:41,310 --> 00:19:42,790
Miss Ketchum?

373
00:19:42,877 --> 00:19:44,835
[gasps]
Oh, policemen.

374
00:19:44,922 --> 00:19:48,143
Okay. I knew
I'd forgotten something. Uh..

375
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:50,319
Okay.

376
00:19:50,406 --> 00:19:51,973
There it is.

377
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:53,801
I thought
for sure I'd sent that.

378
00:19:53,888 --> 00:19:55,846
- Sent what?
- Uh, the class list.

379
00:19:55,933 --> 00:19:58,632
Of the students
in my criminology class.

380
00:19:58,719 --> 00:20:00,155
Your colleague
had asked for it.

381
00:20:00,242 --> 00:20:02,070
And you're chair
of the film club also?

382
00:20:02,157 --> 00:20:04,551
I have that honor.
You know what?

383
00:20:04,638 --> 00:20:07,206
I have the film club register
here as well.

384
00:20:07,293 --> 00:20:10,557
Okay. Yes, yes.

385
00:20:10,644 --> 00:20:11,993
Would you like to see it?

386
00:20:12,080 --> 00:20:14,300
Yes. That would be,
uh, good.

387
00:20:14,387 --> 00:20:16,215
Okay.

388
00:20:16,302 --> 00:20:17,607
Ah, there you go.

389
00:20:21,611 --> 00:20:23,004
And where were you
Tuesday night, Miss Ketchum?

390
00:20:25,136 --> 00:20:27,704
Oh, how thrilling!

391
00:20:27,791 --> 00:20:30,403
- Am I a suspect?
- Are you?

392
00:20:30,490 --> 00:20:32,231
Well..

393
00:20:32,318 --> 00:20:34,972
I'd like to think I can still
summon that kind of passion.

394
00:20:35,059 --> 00:20:37,279
So where were you?

395
00:20:37,366 --> 00:20:39,499
Home. Alone.

396
00:20:39,586 --> 00:20:41,892
Reading a murder mystery,
actually.

397
00:20:41,979 --> 00:20:45,331
Now there's only one name
on both lists. Wesley Blankfein.

398
00:20:45,418 --> 00:20:47,898
Oh, wait.
You just made a face.

399
00:20:47,985 --> 00:20:50,466
Well, he is a sweet boy.

400
00:20:50,553 --> 00:20:52,947
Rather a good actor, actually.

401
00:20:53,034 --> 00:20:56,124
- But, uh, strange.
- Strange? How?

402
00:20:56,211 --> 00:20:57,865
I can't really
put my finger on it.

403
00:20:57,952 --> 00:21:00,868
It's a look in his eyes.

404
00:21:00,955 --> 00:21:02,826
[male #1]
Yep, that's him.

405
00:21:02,913 --> 00:21:05,176
I remember when he moved in.
I mentioned to him

406
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,657
he was a little older
than most of our students

407
00:21:07,744 --> 00:21:09,877
and he said he needed to escape
from his mother.

408
00:21:09,964 --> 00:21:11,270
[laughs]

409
00:21:11,357 --> 00:21:12,706
[clears throat]

410
00:21:12,793 --> 00:21:15,012
Which, uh, I thought
was an odd response.

411
00:21:15,099 --> 00:21:16,492
And when
did you last see him?

412
00:21:16,579 --> 00:21:18,277
- Uh, three weeks ago..
- Excuse me.

413
00:21:18,364 --> 00:21:20,409
Uh, maybe. I figured
he had a girlfriend.

414
00:21:21,932 --> 00:21:24,283
- 'Nothing here.'
- Oh, hey, Dylan.

415
00:21:24,370 --> 00:21:25,936
[Cho]
'Oh, hey, you guys.
Quick question.'

416
00:21:26,023 --> 00:21:27,198
Now you guys said
Marley's boyfriend

417
00:21:27,286 --> 00:21:28,243
waited for her
outside in a car?

418
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:29,940
Yes.

419
00:21:30,027 --> 00:21:31,681
Do you recall
what type of car he drove?

420
00:21:31,768 --> 00:21:34,858
Um, it was black, I think.
I'm bad with cars.

421
00:21:34,945 --> 00:21:36,773
It was a,
it was a black SUV.

422
00:21:36,860 --> 00:21:39,472
- What car did Blankfein drive?
- Uh, he didn't have a car.

423
00:21:41,561 --> 00:21:43,954
Huh. Okay.

424
00:21:44,041 --> 00:21:45,869
Try locating
Blankfein's mother.

425
00:21:45,956 --> 00:21:47,915
Maybe she knows where he is.

426
00:21:48,002 --> 00:21:50,047
Alright. Let me know.

427
00:21:50,134 --> 00:21:51,658
Wesley Blankfein's
in the wind.

428
00:21:51,745 --> 00:21:53,442
Looks like
he might be good for this.

429
00:21:53,529 --> 00:21:54,835
I don't think so.

430
00:21:54,922 --> 00:21:56,227
Marley made contact with me.

431
00:21:56,315 --> 00:21:58,317
The name "Blankfein"
doesn't resonate.

432
00:21:58,404 --> 00:22:00,841
- Marley made contact with you?
- Yes.

433
00:22:00,928 --> 00:22:03,583
Of course. Uh, I think

434
00:22:03,670 --> 00:22:07,108
we might have had enough of your
crime-fighting skills, Kristina.

435
00:22:07,195 --> 00:22:09,240
Might be best to stick
to the crystal therapy

436
00:22:09,328 --> 00:22:12,243
and the, uh...foot massages?

437
00:22:12,331 --> 00:22:13,593
- Reflexology.
- Right.

438
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,159
[phone ringing]
'Reflexology.'

439
00:22:18,249 --> 00:22:20,164
This is Lisbon.

440
00:22:20,251 --> 00:22:22,906
[Fenton]
'Agent Fenton, FBI.
Yeah, we got a case'

441
00:22:22,993 --> 00:22:24,734
here in Lake Tahoe.

442
00:22:24,821 --> 00:22:26,606
Looks like your boy Red John.

443
00:22:26,693 --> 00:22:30,436
Victim's name is
a Jacqueline Sandoval.

444
00:22:30,523 --> 00:22:32,438
'You wanna come take a look?'

445
00:22:37,181 --> 00:22:38,748
You can smile
your arrogant smile

446
00:22:38,835 --> 00:22:40,794
and act like you know
everything about everything

447
00:22:40,881 --> 00:22:42,578
but you don't.

448
00:22:42,665 --> 00:22:44,667
There are whole worlds that you
can't even begin to understand.

449
00:22:44,754 --> 00:22:46,190
Synchronized swimming

450
00:22:46,277 --> 00:22:47,931
is, uh, the only world
that springs to mind.

451
00:22:48,018 --> 00:22:51,457
But I'm sure you're right.
There may be many others.

452
00:22:51,544 --> 00:22:53,807
What's the matter?

453
00:22:53,894 --> 00:22:56,287
Red John killed the woman
who interviewed you.

454
00:22:58,551 --> 00:22:59,856
Oh, my God.

455
00:23:03,773 --> 00:23:05,122
Oh, my God.

456
00:23:12,260 --> 00:23:14,654
[dramatic music]

457
00:23:51,342 --> 00:23:52,474
[indistinct radio chatter]

458
00:23:54,781 --> 00:23:56,522
It's Red John, alright.

459
00:23:56,609 --> 00:23:58,219
Okay, uh, I'll reach out
to the feds.

460
00:23:58,306 --> 00:23:59,655
I'll make sure
they keep us in the loop.

461
00:23:59,742 --> 00:24:01,483
We gotta get back
to Kristina Frye's place.

462
00:24:01,570 --> 00:24:04,312
There are cops all around
her house. Van Pelt is with her

463
00:24:04,399 --> 00:24:07,663
and there's other CBI agents
on their way. She's safe.

464
00:24:07,750 --> 00:24:09,665
I am confident
Red John's not gonna go there.

465
00:24:09,752 --> 00:24:13,539
- That is exactly why he might.
- If he does, we'll get him.

466
00:24:13,626 --> 00:24:15,149
You really wanna hang out
at Kristina's house

467
00:24:15,236 --> 00:24:16,890
waiting for Red John
to show up?

468
00:24:16,977 --> 00:24:18,239
Let's just go back
to the office

469
00:24:18,326 --> 00:24:19,588
and we'll work
the Marley Sparrow case.

470
00:24:19,675 --> 00:24:21,895
There's nothing useful
that I can do there.

471
00:24:21,982 --> 00:24:24,158
This Blankfein character,
he looks good for it, right?

472
00:24:24,245 --> 00:24:26,856
Fine. Go and wait for Red John.

473
00:24:26,943 --> 00:24:29,206
It's not a good idea, though.

474
00:24:29,293 --> 00:24:30,643
Hey, we're in Nevada.

475
00:24:30,730 --> 00:24:34,734
You can't just walk off
and leave me here.

476
00:24:34,821 --> 00:24:37,171
- Hey.
- 'Hey, boss.

477
00:24:37,258 --> 00:24:40,174
So Wesley Blankfein's mother
is Myra Hauser-Blankfein.

478
00:24:40,261 --> 00:24:41,610
Address in Franklin Heights.

479
00:24:41,697 --> 00:24:43,699
And she owns a black SUV
like Grady Shipp drives.

480
00:24:43,786 --> 00:24:45,440
Good. Go check her out.

481
00:24:45,527 --> 00:24:47,529
Now? Well, it's
a long drive.

482
00:24:47,616 --> 00:24:50,010
You leave now,
you'll be there by the morning.

483
00:24:52,316 --> 00:24:54,188
[indistinct radio chatter]

484
00:24:56,756 --> 00:24:59,628
[instrumental music]

485
00:25:10,596 --> 00:25:12,423
Grace, thank you.

486
00:25:18,125 --> 00:25:20,214
How you doing?

487
00:25:20,301 --> 00:25:21,650
I'm doing fine.

488
00:25:24,523 --> 00:25:27,613
Red John certainly
made his point.

489
00:25:27,700 --> 00:25:31,094
Quite possibly,
he'll leave things be now.

490
00:25:31,181 --> 00:25:33,619
I know he will.

491
00:25:33,706 --> 00:25:35,534
I have a clear vision of him.

492
00:25:35,621 --> 00:25:38,145
'He needs to create fear,
that's all.'

493
00:25:38,232 --> 00:25:40,364
He's done that now,
and he feels calm.

494
00:25:40,451 --> 00:25:41,801
'And I'm perfectly safe.'

495
00:25:41,888 --> 00:25:44,064
Will you just stop
that nonsense?

496
00:25:45,805 --> 00:25:47,241
You wanted to promote
your psychic business

497
00:25:47,328 --> 00:25:48,808
and, and you made
a big mistake.

498
00:25:48,895 --> 00:25:51,680
Now will you just,
will you please just own it?

499
00:25:51,767 --> 00:25:53,116
Why are you here?

500
00:25:53,203 --> 00:25:55,162
I am here because
I want to protect you.

501
00:25:55,249 --> 00:25:56,772
And how are you
gonna protect me?

502
00:25:56,859 --> 00:25:58,469
If Red John comes through
that door right now

503
00:25:58,557 --> 00:25:59,819
what are you gonna do,
hypnotize him?

504
00:25:59,906 --> 00:26:02,212
I will do what I need to do.

505
00:26:02,299 --> 00:26:05,259
If Red John wants
to reach me, he will.

506
00:26:05,346 --> 00:26:07,348
I choose to believe
that he doesn't want to.

507
00:26:07,435 --> 00:26:09,698
- Now please, go away.
- I'm gone.

508
00:26:21,623 --> 00:26:22,755
[door closes]

509
00:26:25,627 --> 00:26:27,803
Uh, you're wasting your time.

510
00:26:27,890 --> 00:26:29,849
Ma'am, we're looking
for Mrs. Blankfein and her son.

511
00:26:29,936 --> 00:26:33,026
Gone. And left the cats
to starve. It's not right.

512
00:26:33,113 --> 00:26:34,244
Do you know where they went?

513
00:26:34,331 --> 00:26:37,117
Uh, nope.
Never leaves before. Never.

514
00:26:37,204 --> 00:26:39,859
Every day, 11 o'clock,
like a machine

515
00:26:39,946 --> 00:26:41,861
she's watching her TV shows.

516
00:26:41,948 --> 00:26:46,300
Three days now I hear nothing.
Quiet like the grave.

517
00:26:46,387 --> 00:26:47,867
How about her son Wesley?
Have you seen him?

518
00:26:47,954 --> 00:26:49,216
Nope. Gone, too.

519
00:26:49,303 --> 00:26:50,565
Did it occur to you

520
00:26:50,652 --> 00:26:51,740
that Mrs. Blankfein
might be dead in there?

521
00:26:51,827 --> 00:26:53,873
Yes, it did.

522
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,963
But there'd be a smell,
wouldn't there, if she was dead?

523
00:27:00,053 --> 00:27:02,664
Step back inside,
please, ma'am.

524
00:27:02,751 --> 00:27:04,231
- You good?
- Yeah.

525
00:27:05,928 --> 00:27:07,060
[meowing]

526
00:27:08,496 --> 00:27:10,890
[meowing]

527
00:27:17,113 --> 00:27:20,464
[Wayne]
'Bedroom's clear.'

528
00:27:20,551 --> 00:27:21,640
[Kimball]
'Rigsby.'

529
00:27:26,296 --> 00:27:29,299
Oh, jeez.

530
00:27:29,386 --> 00:27:30,997
"G.S" Grady Shipp.

531
00:27:31,954 --> 00:27:33,086
Bingo.

532
00:27:35,088 --> 00:27:37,307
Inside the mind
of Wesley Blankfein..

533
00:27:37,394 --> 00:27:40,223
- AKA Grady Shipp.
- Not pretty.

534
00:27:40,310 --> 00:27:42,661
It looks like he's obsessed
with Marley

535
00:27:42,748 --> 00:27:44,184
so he builds a shrine

536
00:27:44,271 --> 00:27:46,229
and he fakes up all these photos
of them together.

537
00:27:46,316 --> 00:27:48,014
'Then he tries to turn
the fantasy into reality'

538
00:27:48,101 --> 00:27:50,494
'and posing as Grady Shipp,
he asks her out'

539
00:27:50,581 --> 00:27:53,672
'and she says yes. Big mistake.
Fantasy and reality collide'

540
00:27:53,759 --> 00:27:54,890
and she dies.

541
00:27:54,977 --> 00:27:56,457
[Teresa]
'Sounds about right.'

542
00:27:56,544 --> 00:27:58,981
Where the hell is he?
Uh, where's his mom?

543
00:27:59,068 --> 00:28:00,679
You didn't find anything
useful in the apartment?

544
00:28:00,766 --> 00:28:02,768
- No computer, nothing?
- No. A lot of cats.

545
00:28:02,855 --> 00:28:04,421
Now the pictures of Marley,
they were all taken

546
00:28:04,508 --> 00:28:06,946
at different times and places.
The pictures of Wesley

547
00:28:07,033 --> 00:28:08,817
were all taken
in the same place.

548
00:28:08,904 --> 00:28:10,166
'Nowhere we've been.'

549
00:28:10,253 --> 00:28:11,298
Maybe that's
a safe house for him.

550
00:28:11,385 --> 00:28:13,039
Nothing to say
where it is, though.

551
00:28:13,126 --> 00:28:14,823
- Jane, you wanna take a look?
- Huh?

552
00:28:14,910 --> 00:28:17,826
See if you see anything useful?

553
00:28:17,913 --> 00:28:19,349
Yeah, sure.

554
00:28:19,436 --> 00:28:21,003
If you like.

555
00:28:24,093 --> 00:28:26,966
[instrumental music]

556
00:28:39,587 --> 00:28:41,502
Hmm.

557
00:28:41,589 --> 00:28:44,418
- Yep.
- And..

558
00:28:44,505 --> 00:28:46,550
There's a photo of Wesley
with a sign in the distance

559
00:28:46,637 --> 00:28:48,901
a yellow KC
backward on a pole.

560
00:28:48,988 --> 00:28:51,251
His, his shadow
is pointing right to it.

561
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:57,518
[Wayne]
'Yeah. It's way small
back there, but I see it.'

562
00:28:57,605 --> 00:28:59,694
Yeah, that's the logo
for Kenny's Chili..

563
00:28:59,781 --> 00:29:01,565
Southern California
fast food chain.

564
00:29:01,652 --> 00:29:02,610
There's about 50 or so outlets.

565
00:29:02,697 --> 00:29:04,177
You memorize trademarks?

566
00:29:04,264 --> 00:29:06,570
Well, with Wesley's long shadow
and the golden light

567
00:29:06,657 --> 00:29:09,660
that would say afternoon.
And sun is in the West

568
00:29:09,748 --> 00:29:13,752
so that puts Kenny's
due East of this location

569
00:29:13,839 --> 00:29:15,971
about a block and a half,
I'd say.

570
00:29:16,058 --> 00:29:17,930
Huh. He's right.

571
00:29:18,017 --> 00:29:19,932
50 or so outlets?

572
00:29:20,019 --> 00:29:20,976
Hardware store
and a liquor store

573
00:29:21,063 --> 00:29:22,151
on the block right next to it.

574
00:29:22,238 --> 00:29:23,544
That should narrow it down.

575
00:29:23,631 --> 00:29:24,937
I'll get on it.

576
00:29:26,765 --> 00:29:28,201
- Thank you.
- Oh. No.

577
00:29:30,203 --> 00:29:32,771
You should make that call.

578
00:29:32,858 --> 00:29:34,642
- What call?
- Right.

579
00:29:34,729 --> 00:29:36,644
Like I'm not
a detective, too?

580
00:29:51,877 --> 00:29:54,662
Hey, Jane. It's Grace.
Kristina's taking a nap.

581
00:29:54,749 --> 00:29:56,055
'I can get her for you
if you like.'

582
00:29:56,142 --> 00:29:58,231
I'd appreciate that, Grace.
Thank you.

583
00:30:00,929 --> 00:30:02,061
Kristina?

584
00:30:04,541 --> 00:30:07,066
Kristina,
it's Jane for you.

585
00:30:09,546 --> 00:30:11,113
Open the door.

586
00:30:13,594 --> 00:30:16,379
Kristina? Kristina?

587
00:30:20,557 --> 00:30:23,865
'Kristina?'

588
00:30:23,952 --> 00:30:25,432
'Kristina!'

589
00:30:32,004 --> 00:30:33,309
How did Kristina
get past the guards?

590
00:30:33,396 --> 00:30:35,181
We don't know.
But she also packed a bag

591
00:30:35,268 --> 00:30:37,096
she took her passport
and her credit cards

592
00:30:37,183 --> 00:30:38,880
so we can
assume she wasn't abducted.

593
00:30:38,967 --> 00:30:41,013
No, no, no. You, you,
you can't assume.

594
00:30:41,100 --> 00:30:42,841
Red John could've gotten
in and taken her.

595
00:30:42,928 --> 00:30:44,538
Maybe. But the likelihood is

596
00:30:44,625 --> 00:30:46,279
she panicked
and ran somewhere to hide.

597
00:30:46,366 --> 00:30:48,542
Yeah. Or, or, or maybe
he lured her out somehow.

598
00:30:48,629 --> 00:30:50,631
We'll check
the phone records.

599
00:30:50,718 --> 00:30:52,851
Let's start contacting
her relatives and friends.

600
00:30:52,938 --> 00:30:54,287
She's out there somewhere.

601
00:30:54,374 --> 00:30:56,680
Forgive me, Agent Lisbon,
but belay that order.

602
00:30:56,767 --> 00:30:59,118
The search for Kristina Frye
will now be conducted

603
00:30:59,205 --> 00:31:00,554
by the missing persons unit.

604
00:31:00,641 --> 00:31:01,816
What?

605
00:31:01,903 --> 00:31:03,992
They're the best
at what they do.

606
00:31:04,079 --> 00:31:06,473
They will find her
if she can be found.

607
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:09,563
And, Van Pelt, snap out of it.
Wasn't your fault.

608
00:31:09,650 --> 00:31:11,434
- Yes, ma'am, but--
- 'Move on.'

609
00:31:14,220 --> 00:31:16,439
Alright. Where are we
on the Marley Sparrow case?

610
00:31:16,526 --> 00:31:20,313
We have a suspect at large
by the name of Wesley Blankfein.

611
00:31:20,400 --> 00:31:23,229
He's been obsessed with both
Red John and Marley Sparrow.

612
00:31:23,316 --> 00:31:25,318
He seems to have created
an alter ego

613
00:31:25,405 --> 00:31:27,407
by the name of Grady Shipp.

614
00:31:27,494 --> 00:31:29,322
'It's after a killer
with Red John connections.'

615
00:31:29,409 --> 00:31:31,019
Any leads?

616
00:31:31,106 --> 00:31:32,978
Well, off photos he took, we've
ID'd six possible locations

617
00:31:33,065 --> 00:31:34,980
for what we assume
is Blankfein's safe house.

618
00:31:35,067 --> 00:31:37,025
It's pretty much a long shot,
but it's all we have.

619
00:31:37,112 --> 00:31:38,592
Okay. Alright. Go to it.

620
00:31:38,679 --> 00:31:40,333
Let's start
divvying up the locations.

621
00:31:40,420 --> 00:31:43,466
Cho, you take riverside county.
Bring Rigsby with you.

622
00:31:43,553 --> 00:31:46,513
Van pelt and I will take
the San Bernardino locations.

623
00:31:46,600 --> 00:31:49,820
Jane, you stay here.
Take a break.

624
00:31:49,908 --> 00:31:52,214
- I don't need a break.
- I think you do.

625
00:31:52,301 --> 00:31:54,260
I-I-I'd rather keep active.

626
00:31:54,347 --> 00:31:56,305
You're too hyped up
to be out in the field.

627
00:31:56,392 --> 00:31:58,133
- Oh, that's nonsense.
- I agree with Lisbon.

628
00:31:58,220 --> 00:31:59,613
Get some rest.

629
00:31:59,700 --> 00:32:01,789
Some rest? Oh, just..

630
00:32:01,876 --> 00:32:04,183
[chuckles]
Lie down and catch up
on some Zs.

631
00:32:04,270 --> 00:32:07,403
Kick back with
a good book. Rest?

632
00:32:07,490 --> 00:32:08,796
- I'm fine.
- Debatable.

633
00:32:10,450 --> 00:32:11,668
Do you want me to ask
the psych counselor

634
00:32:11,755 --> 00:32:12,931
for an evaluation?

635
00:32:21,156 --> 00:32:24,029
[dramatic music]

636
00:32:51,491 --> 00:32:54,363
[music continues]

637
00:33:17,865 --> 00:33:20,259
[indistinct chatter]

638
00:33:24,263 --> 00:33:25,394
Sorry.

639
00:33:29,703 --> 00:33:32,488
- 'Tracy, can you mail this?'
- 'Sure. You got it, hon.'

640
00:33:39,495 --> 00:33:40,627
[indistinct chatter]

641
00:33:49,114 --> 00:33:51,203
[Teresa on tape]
'Leave a message.
I'll call you back.'

642
00:33:51,290 --> 00:33:53,596
Lisbon, it's Jane.
Uh, I found it.

643
00:33:53,683 --> 00:33:55,859
It's 52 North Esperanza.

644
00:33:55,946 --> 00:33:59,211
Hotel Del Dorona
in Salinger Mill.

645
00:33:59,298 --> 00:34:01,039
Uh, I am gonna..

646
00:34:03,867 --> 00:34:08,785
Uh, I-I'm gonna wait for you
at, uh, Kenny's okay?

647
00:34:08,872 --> 00:34:11,092
Give me a call
when you get this message.

648
00:34:11,179 --> 00:34:12,311
Thank you.

649
00:34:17,751 --> 00:34:20,101
[instrumental music]

650
00:34:21,102 --> 00:34:24,018
[indistinct chatter]

651
00:34:47,781 --> 00:34:49,870
[music continues]

652
00:34:57,747 --> 00:34:58,922
[grunting]

653
00:35:15,374 --> 00:35:18,028
[sighs]

654
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:19,247
[groaning]

655
00:35:26,341 --> 00:35:27,821
[rustling]

656
00:35:30,128 --> 00:35:31,085
[groaning]

657
00:35:31,172 --> 00:35:32,826
'Welcome, detective.'

658
00:35:35,742 --> 00:35:38,092
I'm Grady Shipp.

659
00:35:38,179 --> 00:35:41,356
'So good of you
to come visit me.'

660
00:35:41,443 --> 00:35:43,837
You're a lucky man.

661
00:35:43,924 --> 00:35:46,448
Very lucky.

662
00:35:46,535 --> 00:35:50,278
Tonight, you will have
the dying honor..

663
00:35:53,063 --> 00:35:55,153
Can we do that again?

664
00:35:56,937 --> 00:35:58,112
Tonight..

665
00:35:59,766 --> 00:36:01,681
...you will have
the honor of dying

666
00:36:02,812 --> 00:36:04,118
'as a sacrifice'

667
00:36:04,205 --> 00:36:07,295
to the holy master,
Red John.

668
00:36:10,298 --> 00:36:13,258
Behold, the blood sacrament

669
00:36:14,302 --> 00:36:15,912
of the master.

670
00:36:17,653 --> 00:36:21,135
Stop. You wanna try
that again?

671
00:36:21,222 --> 00:36:22,789
Huh?

672
00:36:22,876 --> 00:36:25,444
Just t-try it again.
Uh, say it like you mean it.

673
00:36:25,531 --> 00:36:27,489
You know,
where's the passion gone?

674
00:36:27,576 --> 00:36:29,970
Behold the blood sacrament
of the master.

675
00:36:30,057 --> 00:36:33,103
'Oh, n-n-no. I'm not.. I'm not..
I'm not buying it. Come on.'

676
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:34,844
Just, just stop for a sec

677
00:36:34,931 --> 00:36:36,629
and think, think about
what you're doing here

678
00:36:36,716 --> 00:36:39,197
and then we'll start again
from the top, okay?

679
00:36:40,023 --> 00:36:41,808
Uh..

680
00:36:41,895 --> 00:36:43,288
It's alright, Wesley.
I know what's going on.

681
00:36:43,375 --> 00:36:45,464
They've got your mother,
don't they?

682
00:36:46,769 --> 00:36:48,162
Yeah. How'd you know?

683
00:36:48,249 --> 00:36:49,555
They're forcing you
to play a part

684
00:36:49,642 --> 00:36:50,773
in their sick little movie.

685
00:36:50,860 --> 00:36:52,949
Yes.

686
00:36:53,036 --> 00:36:55,909
You're playing the part
of Grady Shipp, right?

687
00:36:56,736 --> 00:36:57,824
Yes.

688
00:36:57,911 --> 00:37:00,043
It's okay. It's okay.

689
00:37:01,044 --> 00:37:03,395
Dylan! Ruth!

690
00:37:05,353 --> 00:37:07,399
We need to talk.

691
00:37:07,486 --> 00:37:11,054
Thank you very much
for totally ruining

692
00:37:11,141 --> 00:37:13,927
a freaking brilliant scene,
you jerk.

693
00:37:14,841 --> 00:37:16,495
Hush, Dyl.

694
00:37:18,410 --> 00:37:20,455
How did you know
it was us?

695
00:37:20,542 --> 00:37:23,110
Well, you were the only people
that mentioned Grady Shipp.

696
00:37:23,197 --> 00:37:24,720
He was your creation.

697
00:37:24,807 --> 00:37:26,461
And it was you
that killed Marley

698
00:37:26,548 --> 00:37:28,550
'wasn't it, Dylan?'

699
00:37:31,031 --> 00:37:33,686
Wesley couldn't hurt a fly.

700
00:37:33,773 --> 00:37:36,254
It was a truly sick individual
that did that.

701
00:37:37,603 --> 00:37:39,735
It was me, actually.

702
00:37:39,822 --> 00:37:41,084
Oh.

703
00:37:41,171 --> 00:37:43,739
'Dyl's much better
with the camera'

704
00:37:43,826 --> 00:37:46,873
and Marley,
deserved what she got.

705
00:37:47,874 --> 00:37:49,658
Pious little bitch.

706
00:37:50,920 --> 00:37:52,357
Keep the camera running.

707
00:37:52,444 --> 00:37:54,881
This is all good stuff.

708
00:37:54,968 --> 00:37:56,186
no offense, but you
wouldn't know good stuff

709
00:37:56,274 --> 00:37:57,579
if it smacked you in the face.

710
00:37:57,666 --> 00:37:59,668
This is just
a corny slasher movie.

711
00:37:59,755 --> 00:38:05,152
Yeah, but real, dude.
Real blood. Real guts.

712
00:38:05,239 --> 00:38:08,329
Yours. Wesley, let's, uh,
wrap this scene up now, okay?

713
00:38:08,416 --> 00:38:09,548
Gonna pick it up
right at the end

714
00:38:09,635 --> 00:38:10,853
behold the blood, etcetera

715
00:38:10,940 --> 00:38:12,638
and then stab
this sucker, okay?

716
00:38:12,725 --> 00:38:13,856
[laughing]

717
00:38:16,032 --> 00:38:18,383
- 'I don't know.'
- That's it.

718
00:38:18,470 --> 00:38:20,167
What? Wh-what are you?
Not.. No!

719
00:38:20,254 --> 00:38:22,648
Okay, this, this man is dead.
Okay, the only question is

720
00:38:22,735 --> 00:38:25,651
'whether you and your mom want
to live or you want to die'

721
00:38:25,738 --> 00:38:27,174
'like him, okay?
That's your choice here.'

722
00:38:27,261 --> 00:38:29,002
These people are nuttier
than a fruitcake.

723
00:38:29,089 --> 00:38:31,047
'They're gonna kill
you regardless.'

724
00:38:31,134 --> 00:38:34,137
- 'You don't have to do this.'
- We are not monsters, Wesley.

725
00:38:35,225 --> 00:38:36,531
We're artists!

726
00:38:37,706 --> 00:38:39,665
'We are making art.'

727
00:38:41,493 --> 00:38:42,581
When the movie's done
of course

728
00:38:42,668 --> 00:38:44,887
you and your mom
are free to go

729
00:38:44,974 --> 00:38:47,716
with our gratitude
for your help.

730
00:38:47,803 --> 00:38:49,327
Stay calm.

731
00:38:50,589 --> 00:38:52,547
Behold the blood.
Wesley.

732
00:38:59,859 --> 00:39:01,339
I'm sorry.

733
00:39:01,426 --> 00:39:03,906
Wesley.
Wesley, Wesley, hey.

734
00:39:03,993 --> 00:39:05,952
- Behold..
- No, Wesley.

735
00:39:06,039 --> 00:39:07,562
The blood sacrament..

736
00:39:07,649 --> 00:39:08,607
- No. It's okay.
- 'Of the master!'

737
00:39:08,694 --> 00:39:09,651
Wesley!

738
00:39:09,738 --> 00:39:12,045
[gunshot]

739
00:39:12,132 --> 00:39:13,307
[groaning]

740
00:39:15,875 --> 00:39:17,006
[groaning]

741
00:39:19,052 --> 00:39:20,706
[grunting]

742
00:39:23,578 --> 00:39:24,710
[panting]

743
00:39:26,581 --> 00:39:29,105
No. No.. No!

744
00:39:29,192 --> 00:39:30,890
No, no!

745
00:39:30,977 --> 00:39:32,674
[grunting]

746
00:39:32,761 --> 00:39:35,895
No! No!

747
00:39:35,982 --> 00:39:37,984
[Red John]
'If there's one thing
I can't tolerate'

748
00:39:38,071 --> 00:39:40,203
'it's cheap imitations
of my work.'

749
00:39:41,030 --> 00:39:42,205
[grunting]

750
00:39:43,772 --> 00:39:45,861
[grunting]

751
00:39:49,865 --> 00:39:51,040
Oh.

752
00:39:57,177 --> 00:39:58,352
[panting]

753
00:40:04,140 --> 00:40:05,925
'Do you know who I am?'

754
00:40:07,274 --> 00:40:08,667
Yes.

755
00:40:25,205 --> 00:40:27,599
[dramatic music]

756
00:40:28,991 --> 00:40:31,429
"Tiger, tiger,
burning bright

757
00:40:32,517 --> 00:40:34,432
"in the forests
of the night

758
00:40:35,824 --> 00:40:37,696
